## stage1 / stage3 — why these fail here

The failures are in the clipboard path. The app writes its selection to
`navigator.clipboard` and the harness reads it back; on this host the page's
clipboard writes do not reach the harness (the read-back still holds a previous
value, e.g. `10.069`), so every later check that depends on a paste cascades.
The same 15 stage1 checks and the same 4 stage3 checks fail, with identical
messages, at:

- baseline `52e8a79` (fresh build in a worktree),
- Phase 3E `2695b65` (fresh build in a worktree),
- the live Pages site (`LIVE=1`),
- this branch.

So the failures are independent of this branch. They are not counted as PASS.
CI runs the same suites on Linux with `CHROME_PATH=/usr/bin/google-chrome`;
that run is the one that will establish their status (WO-08).

## ui_compact — sandbox workaround

Running every part in one browser process crashed the browser
(`browserContext.newPage: … has been closed`) while opening the next context.
The harness header says the sandbox runs Chromium single-process and the run is
meant to be split; run that way (PART=ui, PART=panels; then PART=mobile with
`WIDTHS=390` and `WIDTHS=320`), all 63 checks pass with 0 failures.

## Harness change made for the autosave envelope (not a product test change)

Phase 3B / 3B-corrective seed the app's autosave record by hand. Since WO-01 the
record is a revision envelope (`{ format: 'sigrun-autosave', revision, savedAt,
payload }`); the seeding helpers in `tools/e2e_phase3_3b.cjs` and
`tools/e2e_phase3_3b_corrective.cjs` now unwrap/wrap it. No check was removed,
renamed or relaxed: the same assertions (two models saved, then the blocked
interval bases) run on both sides. Before the change the branch failed
`the autosave holds both models for the seeded state`; after it, 41/41 and 13/13
pass — matching the baseline's 41/41 and 13/13.
